  "id": "COMPOUND:30682 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387, a compound that is a target of multiple entities, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, and Npc13565. All of these entities ultimately target VMRC-LCP, suggesting a shared mechanism of action or a common downstream pathway. The evidence indicates that Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside may act as a modulator of SNU-387, which in turn influences VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside to influence VMRC-LCP via a complex network of targets, possibly through the activation or inhibition of downstream signaling pathways. This suggests a possible role in cellular processes involving VMRC-LCP, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
